# tests/clojure-suite/MANIFEST.sha256
#
# SHA-256 manifest of every vendored Clojure test-suite file under
# tests/clojure-suite/vendor/. This is the anti-cheating device for the
# no-edit rule: vendored files must stay byte-identical to the tagged
# upstream release. `tools/verify-vendor.sh` re-hashes every file listed
# below and fails (non-zero exit) on any mismatch, missing file, or
# extra un-manifested file in vendor/.
#
# Upstream source (PRIMARY -- 48 of the 51 files below):
#   repo:   https://github.com/clojure/clojure
#   tag:    clojure-1.13.0-alpha6
#   commit: 15c821d7e7df241c8f9fed42fbc51b09c65b67d9
#   path:   test/clojure/test_clojure/*.clj  (top-level files, PLUS a
#           small set of subdirectory companion files that a vendored
#           top-level file genuinely `:require`s -- see "Companion
#           namespaces" below. Every other subdirectory file is a
#           support/fixture file for an excluded JVM-bound suite; see
#           tests/clojure-suite/NOT-PORTABLE.md for what and why)
#
# Upstream source (SECOND REPO -- the 3 spec files, added by SPEC-W6b):
#   repo:        https://github.com/clojure/spec.alpha
#   describe:    v0.6.249-2-g6b698ee  (the 0.6.250-SNAPSHOT line)
#   spec-commit: 6b698eed1787c14907082c86de3410dd51e816b4
#   path:        src/test/clojure/clojure/test_clojure/*.clj
#   files:       instr.clj, multi_spec.clj, spec.clj
#
#   A second repo, not a second STANDARD. `clojure.spec.alpha` lives in
#   its own git repository but it is not a third-party library: it SHIPS
#   WITH Clojure -- `clojure -Sdeps '{:deps {org.clojure/clojure
#   {:mvn/version "1.13.0-alpha6"}}}'` gives you a working
#   `clojure.spec.alpha` with no other dependency -- and these three
#   files ARE that library's official test suite. They sit at exactly the
#   `clojure/test_clojure/` path the primary repo's own suite uses and
#   declare `clojure.test-clojure.{spec,instr,multi-spec}` namespaces.
#   They are vendored under identical rules to everything else here:
#   byte-identical, hash-locked, never hand-edited, flat in vendor/ (the
#   runner derives each file's module path from its own `(ns ...)` form,
#   not from the filename). `multi_spec.clj` `:require`s
#   `[clojure.test-clojure.spec :refer [submap?]]`, which resolves
#   because `spec.clj` is vendored beside it and materializes as
#   `clojure/test_clojure/spec.mova` in the runner's scratch tree -- the
#   same mechanism the "Companion namespaces" block below describes, with
#   no flattening needed.
#
#   NOTE for tools/oracle-census.sh: it reads the primary upstream commit
#   with `grep -m1 '^#\s*commit:'`, which is why the key above is spelled
#   `spec-commit:` -- the primary `commit:` line must stay the first one.
#
# Companion namespaces (flattened into vendor/ under a
# `<parent>_<child>.clj` name, e.g. `protocols/examples.clj` ->
# `protocols_examples.clj`; the runner derives each vendored file's
# module path from its own `(ns ...)` form, not from this filename, so
# the flattening is cosmetic only -- see tools/clojure-suite-run.bb):
#   protocols_examples.clj       <- protocols/examples.clj
#     (required by protocols.clj's `:use`)
#   protocols_more_examples.clj  <- protocols/more_examples.clj
#     (required by protocols.clj's `:require ... :as other`)
#   repl_example.clj             <- repl/example.clj
#     (required by repl.clj's `:use`)
#
# Counts (recorded here, not just in NOT-PORTABLE.md's prose, so
# tools/generate-compat-report.bb can read the "N of M vendored, K
# excluded" arithmetic from an artifact that survives into a fresh
# checkout -- the pinned upstream clone used to derive these numbers is a
# session-scratchpad path that will NOT exist on a later machine/run):
#   upstream-top-level-clj-files: 67
#   vendored-count: 45
#   excluded-count: 22
#   companion-count: 3
#   spec-alpha-count: 3
#   (67 = 45 + 22 top-level files of the PRIMARY repo; the 3 companions
#   above are additional subdirectory files of that same repo, and the 3
#   spec-alpha files come from the SECOND repo -- neither group is part
#   of the 67/45/22 top-level arithmetic, and both physically live in
#   vendor/, so the directory holds 45 + 3 + 3 = 51 files. Every excluded
#   top-level file is named with a reason in
#   tests/clojure-suite/NOT-PORTABLE.md)
#
# Regenerate (do NOT hand-edit) with:
#   cd tests/clojure-suite/vendor && shasum -a 256 *.clj | sort -k2 >> MANIFEST.sha256
# (after re-copying files byte-identically from the pinned upstream tree
# and re-writing this header).
#
# Format below: standard `shasum -a 256 -c` checksum lines, one per
# vendored file, sorted by filename. Lines starting with '#' are comments
# and ignored by `shasum -c`.
